{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.EkParitySplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.EkParitySplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Hom.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.massProj_barOrth_decayProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.massProj_barOrth_decayProj","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L160-L170","doc":"**Mass ⊥ decay under the Gram form.** The mass (bar-even) and decay\n(bar-odd) projections of any elements are orthogonal under every\n`σ`-invariant pairing `B` — the structural reason the Frobenius/Gram\nsignature splits along the bar parity (the decay ghost mode occupies its\nown block). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barEven_barOdd_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barEven_barOdd_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L145-L158","doc":"**Bar-even ⊥ bar-odd.** For a pairing `B` additive in its second slot and\ninvariant under the involution `σ`, a `σ`-fixed vector `e` and a\n`σ`-negated vector `o` are `B`-orthogonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.decayProj_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.decayProj_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L122-L131","doc":"**Non-vacuity (generic / categorical, §7c — no `ℂ`).** The decay (bar-odd)\nface is nonzero *exactly* when `f` is not bar-even. In the canonical instance\n`R = LaurentPolynomial ℚ`, `σ : q ↦ q⁻¹` (the bar) and `f = e_k(q,q³,…)`:\nsince `e_k` is not palindromic (`σ f ≠ f`, verified numerically in\n`qbeta_c3_barodd_tetraplectic_reduction_probe.py`), `decayProj σ f ≠ 0` —\nthe sinh/decay/`S` carrier genuinely holds content, without leaving the\ncategorical ring `R` for the archimedean `ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.decayProj_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.decayProj_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L109-L120","doc":"**Decay part vanishes iff `f` is bar-even** (`σ`-fixed). The mass face\n(self-conjugate / real) is exactly the kernel of the decay projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sigma_decayProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sigma_decayProj","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L98-L107","doc":"**Decay projection is bar-odd** (`σ`-negated / sinh). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sigma_massProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sigma_massProj","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L88-L96","doc":"**Mass projection is bar-even** (`σ`-fixed / cosh). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.massProj_sub_decayProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.massProj_sub_decayProj","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The `σ`-partner is recovered as the difference:\n`massProj f − decayProj f = σ f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.massProj_add_decayProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.massProj_add_decayProj","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L75-L79","doc":"The two projections reconstruct `f`: `massProj f + decayProj f = f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.two_mul_decayProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.two_mul_decayProj","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.two_mul_massProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.two_mul_massProj","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L59-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.decayProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.decayProj","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L53-L57","doc":"**Decay (sinh / bar-odd) projection** under a ring involution `σ`:\n`½(f − σ f)`. On `|q| = 1` (`σ = conj`) this is `i·Im f` — the phase /\ndecay / Q_β `c₃` bar-odd `S` face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.massProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.massProj","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EkParitySplit.lean#L47-L51","doc":"**Mass (cosh / bar-even) projection** under a ring involution `σ`:\n`½(f + σ f)`. On `|q| = 1` (`σ = conj`) this is `Re f` — the real / mass /\n`−Vol(4₁)` face. ","signatureChunk":0}]}